"""Additional original explanation text for technical and decision questions."""
def extend(terms):
    def t(key,label,why):
        terms[key]=(label,why)
    t('pretrain','Pretraining','Learns broad statistical representations from a large corpus before downstream adaptation. The precise objective depends on architecture and modality.')
    t('selfsupervised','Self-supervised learning','Derives training targets from the data itself, such as predicting held-out or next tokens, rather than requiring a human label for every example.')
    t('attention','Self-attention','Builds context-dependent representations by weighting permitted relationships between tokens. Causal masking can restrict which positions are visible.')
    t('position','Positional information','Encodes sequence order or relative position so attention can distinguish arrangements of the same tokens. Implementations vary by architecture.')
    t('autoregressive','Autoregressive generation','Predicts successive output elements conditioned on preceding context. Efficient serving can reuse cached intermediate states rather than recomputing everything.')
    t('tokenizer','Tokenizer','Maps supported text units into token IDs and back. Tokens can be words, subwords, characters, or byte-derived units depending on the tokenizer.')
    t('embedding','Embedding representation','Maps supported content to numeric vectors useful for similarity or other downstream tasks. Similarity is model-dependent and is not proof of factual equivalence.')
    t('weights','Model weights','Are learned numerical parameters adjusted during training. Supplying a normal inference request does not inherently update them.')
    t('logits','Logits','Are unnormalized token scores that can be transformed and normalized for next-token selection. They are not usage logs or security permissions.')
    t('softmax','Softmax','Transforms a vector of scores into normalized positive values summing to one in exact arithmetic. It does not validate truth or implement content moderation.')
    t('vocab','Tokenizer vocabulary','Defines token IDs available to the tokenizer. Its size is different from the number of tokens allowed in one request.')
    t('sft','Supervised fine-tuning','Adapts supported models using curated examples of inputs and desired outputs. Independent evaluation is needed to check generalization and regressions.')
    t('rlhf','Reinforcement learning from human feedback','Uses preference feedback to guide model behavior, often through a learned reward model and policy optimization. It does not guarantee safety or truth.')
    t('reward','Reward model','Predicts a preference or reward signal from labeled feedback in applicable alignment workflows. It is a proxy whose biases and errors need evaluation.')
    t('greedy','Greedy next-token selection','Chooses a highest-scoring permitted next token at each decoding step. It can still produce false, malformed, or inappropriate output.')
    t('topk','Top-k sampling','Restricts next-token candidates to a configured number of top-ranked tokens where supported. It does not impose a plain-language vocabulary policy.')
    t('eos','End-of-sequence condition','A model-generated termination token can end generation before a maximum length is reached. Other termination conditions can also apply.')
    t('stop','Configured stop sequence','A supported generated delimiter can terminate a response. A naive delimiter such as a closing brace can truncate nested JSON or omit required syntax.')
    t('schema','Supported structured output plus schema validation','Constrains output structure where supported and checks the returned object before use. Correct structure does not imply correct facts or authorized actions.')
    t('quant','Quantization','Uses lower-precision representations to reduce model memory or compute requirements. Quality and runtime compatibility must be measured; savings do not prove hardware fit.')
    t('lora','Low-rank adaptation (LoRA)','Trains low-rank adaptation parameters in a supported fine-tuning setup while typically freezing base weights. It reduces trainable parameter count but does not guarantee unchanged behavior.')
    t('overfit','Overfitting','Fits training-specific patterns too closely and generalizes poorly. A gap between training and independent evaluation can indicate this problem.')
    t('forget','Catastrophic forgetting','Occurs when adaptation degrades previously learned capabilities. Diagnose using broad regression tests rather than assuming any small dataset necessarily causes it.')
    t('epoch','Training epoch','Is one pass over the designated training dataset under the training setup. It is not the number of examples processed in an individual update.')
    t('batch','Training batch','Is a group of examples processed together in a training step or accumulation scheme. Batch size is not a context-window limit.')
    t('corpus','Training corpus','Is the collection of source material used for training. Its quality, provenance, coverage, and permissions affect the resulting model and risk.')
    t('gan','Generator–discriminator training','Uses a generator and an adversarial discriminator in a GAN. This is distinct from diffusion denoising and transformer language generation.')
    t('modecollapse','Mode collapse','Is loss of output diversity in a generative training process, particularly associated with GANs. It is not simply loss of conversation history.')
    t('perplexity','Perplexity on a comparable evaluation setup','Measures token predictive fit for a language model on a specified dataset. It is not a general guarantee of helpfulness, factuality, or comparability across tokenizers.')
    t('bleu','BLEU','Uses reference n-gram overlap, commonly for translation evaluation. Low overlap can reflect wording differences and does not independently establish factual error.')
    t('rouge','ROUGE','Uses reference overlap, commonly for summarization assessment. It should be complemented with factual, safety, and human-quality checks.')
    t('ttft','Time to first token','Measures initial response delay before the first token becomes available under the measurement definition. It differs from complete-response latency.')
    t('throughput','Output token generation rate','Measures output production speed under the stated conditions. It is distinct from first-token delay and content correctness.')
    t('local','Controlled local deployment of a compatible licensed model','Can meet an offline requirement if all needed model files, runtimes, tools, and dependencies are available locally. Open weights, quantization, and GPUs are not universal logical requirements.')
    t('retention','Review service-specific retention and data-use terms','Checks logs, abuse monitoring, training use, deletion, account settings, and contracts. Frozen model weights alone do not establish zero retention.')
    t('chunk','Coherent document chunking','Splits sources into useful retrieval units while preserving sufficient meaning and metadata. Chunk boundaries influence retrieval relevance and answer context.')
    t('hybrid','Hybrid lexical and vector retrieval','Combines exact-term matching with semantic similarity. It is useful for identifiers and paraphrases, subject to relevance and access evaluation.')
    t('rerank','Rerank retrieved candidates','Rescores an initial result set for relevance. It cannot promote a document that never entered the candidate set.')
    t('citations','Verify claims against cited source passages','Checks whether a citation actually supports the output. A plausible URL or citation marker is not proof of grounding.')
    t('abstain','Abstain or escalate when evidence is insufficient','Avoids inventing a consequential answer when approved context lacks support. Defined user messaging and review routes improve usefulness.')
    t('refresh','Refresh and govern the retrieval index','Updates approved evidence, removes or marks obsolete versions, and preserves source authorization. New documents alone do not prove retrieval and generation quality.')
    t('precision','Retrieval precision','Measures how much of a returned set is relevant. It differs from recall and from whether an answer is faithful to its evidence.')
    t('recall','Retrieval recall','Measures how much of the relevant evidence is found under a defined benchmark. It requires a suitable relevance reference set.')
    t('groundcheck','Evaluate answer groundedness','Checks whether generated claims are supported by supplied evidence. Relevant retrieval alone does not establish this property.')
    t('heldout','Independent representative evaluation','Uses cases not used to design or train the change, including important user groups and failure cases. It supports regression detection rather than merely memorization.')
    t('judge','Calibrate automated judging with expert review','Checks a model-based evaluator for agreement, bias, and failure cases instead of treating the judge as ground truth.')
    t('contextbudget','Budget and select relevant context','Reserves capacity for instructions, evidence, history, and generation according to model-specific limits. Exceeding a limit may cause rejection or configured truncation, not a universal oldest-message deletion rule.')
    t('summary','Validated history compaction','Replaces verbose history with checked summaries and important factual state. Summaries can lose or distort details and need verification.')
    t('history','Governed application-managed conversation state','Stores and supplies relevant history where needed without implying model-weight updates. Stateful platform features and their retention policies must be reviewed separately.')
    t('promptversion','Version prompts and regression-test revisions','Makes instruction changes identifiable, comparable, and reversible. A version label is useful only when actual content and dependencies are tracked.')
    t('specific','Specify audience, task, constraints, and output expectations','Makes a request actionable without relying on vague demands for better output. It does not replace validation or permissions.')
    t('delimiter','Clearly separate instructions from untrusted source content','Reduces ambiguity and marks external material as data. Delimiters alone are not a security boundary.')
    t('functionvalidate','Authorize and validate tool calls before execution','Checks the caller, action, arguments, and business policy in trusted code. The model proposes a call; it does not itself grant permission.')
    t('toolresult','Validate tool results before downstream use','Checks schema, plausibility, status, and policy. A successful HTTP status does not guarantee a correct business result.')
    t('idempotent','Protect repeated actions with durable idempotency','Maps repeated requests for the same logical action to one intended effect where the external system supports it. A new key on every retry defeats duplicate protection.')
    t('timeout','Bound waits and use safe failure handling','Limits stalled work and communicates failure or escalation. Local timeout or cancellation does not prove that a remote operation was rolled back.')
    t('bounded','Enforce task, tool-call, and spending budgets','Bounds autonomous work and delegation. A stopping condition is separate from content moderation or prompt length.')
    t('approval','Human approval before a consequential action','Places a qualified decision before the external effect with proper correlation and authorization. Reviewing afterward cannot undo every side effect.')
    t('draftreview','Draft with AI and retain accountable review','Uses generation for candidate content while qualified people or validated controls check correctness, rights, and appropriateness.')
    t('parallel','Parallelize independent work with a controlled join','Can reduce duration when branches are independent and resource limits permit. Dependent work still follows its prerequisites.')
    t('sequential','Order dependent workflow stages','Ensures later steps receive validated earlier outputs. Parallelizing a dependency can produce incomplete or incorrect work.')
    t('cache','Governed response caching','Reuses eligible results only within appropriate identity, freshness, and semantic boundaries. Similar wording alone does not make a cached answer safe.')
    t('promptcache','Supported prompt-prefix caching','Can reuse eligible repeated prefix processing under provider-specific rules. It is not the same as serving a previously generated final answer.')
    t('escalate','Route uncertain or out-of-scope cases to an authorized specialist','Prevents an assistant from pretending to have authority or evidence it lacks. The handoff should preserve necessary permitted context.')
    t('schemaextract','Extract, validate, and reconcile structured fields','Combines supported extraction with checks against source evidence and business rules. Valid JSON alone does not establish field accuracy.')
    t('recommend','Use a recommendation or predictive component when appropriate','Selects or ranks candidates using suitable data and evaluation. It need not be replaced by open-ended language generation.')
    t('codecheck','Review, test, and scan generated code before use','Treats generated software as an untrusted candidate rather than guaranteed functional or secure output.')
    t('scope','Define permitted tasks and non-goals','Sets business and agent boundaries before granting tools or autonomy. Behavioral descriptions still need technical enforcement.')
    t('identity','Separate workload identities and least-privilege permissions','Reduces authority sharing and lateral movement. A shared highly privileged key undermines isolation.')
    t('injection','Prompt injection through untrusted instructions','Attempts to redirect model behavior using user input or external content. Merely reading suspicious text does not guarantee that an attack succeeds.')
    t('indirect','Indirect prompt injection','Places hostile instructions in retrieved documents or tool content rather than directly in the user request. Treat source material as untrusted data.')
    t('poison','Training or adaptation data poisoning','Manipulates learning data to influence model behavior. This differs from an inference-time instruction attack.')
    t('dlp','Detect and limit sensitive-data exposure','Uses suitable discovery, redaction, access, and delivery controls. A word blacklist alone cannot identify every sensitive fact.')
    t('network','Configure supported private connectivity and network controls','Limits network paths when correctly configured. Private routing does not replace authentication or make the whole solution absolutely isolated.')
    t('secrets','Keep secrets in controlled secret storage and execution code','Avoids placing raw credentials in model context, repositories, or logs. Scope secret access to authorized workloads.')
    t('audit','Protected audit trails and traceability','Records necessary actions, versions, and approvals for investigation while controlling sensitive telemetry access and retention.')
    t('rights','Review rights, licenses, and permitted content use','Checks source and output obligations rather than assuming AI generation removes intellectual-property restrictions.')
    t('incident','Use a tested incident response and containment process','Defines owners, detection, containment, evidence handling, recovery, and communication rather than treating an alert as the end of response.')
    t('redteam','Adversarial and misuse-oriented testing','Probes likely bypasses and harmful interactions before and after release. Passing a finite test suite is not proof that all attacks are prevented.')
    t('saferelease','Stage deployment with quality gates and rollback','Limits initial exposure and promotes only when defined outcomes remain acceptable. Availability alone does not establish answer quality.')
    t('deletion','Apply deletion across governed data copies and indexes','Tracks source data, retrieval indexes, caches, logs, and memory where required. Deleting one visible file does not prove every retained copy is gone.')
    t('risk','Assess impact, likelihood, affected users, and mitigations','Prioritizes controls in proportion to potential harm rather than using the same autonomy for every workflow.')
    t('fairtest','Test subgroup outcomes and investigate disparities','Uses relevant, appropriate comparisons and review rather than inferring fairness from one aggregate score.')
    t('explain','Provide meaningful decision factors and reviewable evidence','Helps stakeholders understand a recommendation without claiming that a fluent generated rationale is the model real internal causal explanation.')
    t('noretain','Do not infer zero retention from frozen weights','Separates parameter learning from service logging, stored history, caches, and contractual data use. Inference and retention are different questions.')
    t('readiness','Assess data, skills, workflow, infrastructure, and control readiness','Identifies gaps before scaling a business idea. Access to a model alone does not establish operational preparedness.')
    t('portfolio','Balance opportunities by value, feasibility, and risk','Avoids concentrating investment solely on novelty or on whichever demo is most impressive.')
    t('baseline','Establish pre-change business performance','Makes improvement measurable against comparable conditions rather than attributing every later change to AI.')
    t('experiment','Compare a pilot with an appropriate control or baseline','Helps separate the effect of the intervention from seasonality and unrelated changes. Experiment design must be ethical and appropriate.')
    t('qualitycost','Compare cost per verified acceptable outcome','Accounts for success rates, rework, review, and full workflow costs rather than only unit model pricing.')
    t('buildbuy','Compare a prebuilt solution with custom development against requirements','Considers fit, integration, time, ownership, controls, and total cost. Neither custom nor prebuilt is always superior.')
    t('sponsor','Assign an accountable business sponsor and decision rights','Connects funding, outcomes, and adoption ownership rather than leaving a pilot as an unowned technical experiment.')
    t('roadmap','Use a phased roadmap with measurable stage gates','Links pilot learning to incremental expansion or stopping decisions rather than promising immediate organization-wide automation.')
    t('workflow','Redesign the workflow around verified outcomes and human roles','Avoids merely placing a chatbot on top of an unchanged broken process. Explicit responsibilities and exceptions matter.')
    t('training','Provide role-specific training and approved-use guidance','Builds practical capability and awareness of limits. Tool access alone does not mean users can apply it safely.')
    t('feedback','Collect reviewed user feedback and verified outcomes','Turns field issues into improvements without treating popularity as proof of correctness.')
    t('adoptionmetric','Measure sustained appropriate use and task success','Distinguishes installed seats or trial logins from useful adoption. Usage must be interpreted with quality and risk.')
    t('scale','Scale only after operational, economic, and control criteria pass','Requires support, capacity, quality, and governance evidence, not just a successful demonstration.')
    t('exit','Define stopping, switching, and decommissioning criteria','Protects against continuing a project because of sunk costs or indefinite vendor dependence.')
    t('sustain','Consider resource efficiency alongside required quality','Evaluates whether a smaller or less wasteful solution meets the need. Lower compute alone does not excuse unacceptable quality or harm.')
    t('procure','Evaluate contractual, data, service, and exit terms','Assesses the actual provider and offering rather than relying only on branding or a model leaderboard.')
    t('dataproduct','Assign authoritative data ownership and freshness responsibilities','Ensures knowledge quality remains accountable after deployment. Adding documents without ownership can create conflicting evidence.')
    t('unitcost','Track variable usage and fixed operating cost separately','Supports capacity and budget planning under changing demand. A token-price reduction need not reduce the total bill if usage grows.')
    t('realized','Distinguish estimated capacity savings from realized business benefit','Saved minutes do not automatically become reduced payroll or revenue. Validate how released capacity is actually used.')
    t('tradeoff','Evaluate objectives and constraints together','Balances usefulness, speed, cost, privacy, and safety instead of maximizing one metric without boundaries.')
    t('pay3','3 months','For $24,000 upfront cost and $8,000 net monthly benefit, simple payback is $24,000 / $8,000 = 3 months, assuming constant benefits and ignoring discounting.')
    t('pay2','2 months','A two-month payback would require cumulative net benefit to reach the initial cost after two months; use net rather than gross benefit.')
    t('pay4','4 months','A four-month payback means cumulative net benefit reaches the initial investment at month four under the stated assumptions.')
    t('pay6','6 months','A six-month payback requires cumulative net benefit to offset the initial investment by month six.')
    t('roi25','25%','For $150,000 benefit and $120,000 total cost over the same period, simple ROI is ($150,000 - $120,000) / $120,000 = 25%.')
    t('roi20','20%','A 20% ROI means net benefit is one fifth of the total cost. Dividing net benefit by gross benefit instead uses the wrong ROI denominator.')
    t('roi125','125%','A gross-benefit-to-cost ratio of 125% is not the same as 125% net ROI. Subtract cost before computing net ROI.')
    t('roi80','80%','An 80% ROI means net benefit equals 0.8 times total cost; it is not obtained by dividing cost by gross benefit.')
    t('time25','25% time reduction','Reducing handling time from 12 to 9 minutes saves 3 / 12 = 25% of the baseline time. Use the original duration as denominator.')
    t('time33','About 33.3% time reduction','A one-third time reduction means saving one third of the original duration. Dividing saved time by the new duration answers a different question.')
    t('time75','75% time reduction','A 75% time reduction leaves only a quarter of baseline duration. The share remaining is different from the share saved.')
    t('time3','3% time reduction','A three-minute change is not automatically a three-percent change; percentage change depends on baseline duration.')
    t('total900','$900 per month','At $500 in model charges, $250 in review, and $150 in monitoring per month, listed recurring cost is $500 + $250 + $150 = $900.')
    t('total500','$500 per month','A model-only charge may omit human review, monitoring, and other recurring workflow costs.')
    t('total750','$750 per month','A subtotal can omit an operating category; include every listed cost once when calculating total recurring cost.')
    t('total650','$650 per month','Adding only selected operating costs is not a complete total when other recurring categories are specified.')
    t('accepta','Model A: about $0.033 per accepted answer','With independent one-call outcomes and no extra costs, $0.03 / 0.90 is about $0.033 per accepted answer, below $0.02 / 0.50 = $0.04 for Model B.')
    t('acceptb','Model B: $0.02 per accepted answer','The $0.02 call price must be divided by acceptance rate to calculate cost per accepted answer; it is not already the accepted-outcome cost.')
    t('accepttie','Both models have the same cost per accepted answer','Equal accepted-outcome cost requires equal call-price-to-acceptance ratios under the simplified assumptions.')
    t('acceptnone','Acceptance rate is irrelevant to outcome cost','Rejected attempts still consume resources, so acceptance rate matters when comparing verified outcomes.')
    t('net14','$14,000 monthly net benefit','$20,000 in verified monthly benefit minus $6,000 recurring monthly operating cost yields $14,000 monthly net benefit, before other unspecified costs.')
    t('net20','$20,000 monthly net benefit','Gross monthly benefit is not net benefit when recurring operating costs are specified.')
    t('net26','$26,000 monthly net benefit','Adding recurring cost to gross benefit does not calculate net benefit; net benefit subtracts costs.')
    t('net6','$6,000 monthly net benefit','Recurring operating cost by itself is not the remaining net benefit after subtracting cost from benefit.')
    t('capacity100','100 hours of released capacity per month','Saving 5 minutes on each of 1,200 tasks gives 6,000 minutes, or 100 hours. This is capacity, not automatically cash savings.')
    t('capacity6000','6,000 hours of released capacity per month','Minutes must be divided by 60 to express hours. Keeping the minute total while labeling it hours creates a unit error.')
    t('capacity20','20 hours of released capacity per month','Calculate saved minutes per task times task volume before converting to hours; converting volume alone does not measure time savings.')
    t('capacity5','5 hours of released capacity per month','A per-task minute saving is not the total monthly hours. The task count and unit conversion are required.')
    t('pct15','15% successful completion rate','Successful completions divided by the stated denominator gives a completion rate; choose the denominator appropriate to the question.')
    t('pct60','60% successful completion rate','For 600 successful completions from 1,000 attempts, the rate is 600 / 1,000 = 60%. Purchased-seat count is not the attempted-task denominator.')
    t('pct40','40% successful completion rate','Failures divided by attempts give a failure rate, not successful completion rate, when the categories are exhaustive.')
    t('pct100','100% successful completion rate','All attempted tasks would need to be successful for a 100% completion rate; adoption or licensing alone does not imply that.')
    t('costdouble','Total variable cost doubles','With constant workload mix, tripled volume and a unit cost of two thirds of baseline yield 3 × 2/3 = 2 times baseline total variable cost.')
    t('costless','Total variable cost falls by one third','A one-third unit-price decrease does not imply a one-third total-bill decrease when usage also changes.')
    t('costsame','Total variable cost stays unchanged','An unchanged bill requires usage growth and unit-cost changes to exactly offset one another.')
    t('costtriple','Total variable cost triples','Tripled usage only triples cost if the unit cost stays unchanged, holding other factors constant.')
    t('budget80','80,000 requests per month','A $4,000 variable budget divided by $0.05 per request funds 80,000 requests, ignoring fixed costs and rounding restrictions.')
    t('budget200','200 requests per month','Multiplying a currency budget by per-request currency cost does not produce request capacity; divide budget by unit cost.')
    t('budget4000','4,000 requests per month','A dollar budget is not numerically a request count unless unit cost happens to be one dollar per request.')
    t('budget8000','8,000 requests per month','Check decimal placement when dividing budget by a fractional-dollar unit cost.')
